{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"fish_giant_catfish","model_identifier":"fish_giant_catfish","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# fish_giant_catfish\n\nGiant catfish (B8), 1.8 m (64 u). Deepwoods pools.\n\nDark mottled grey-green, wide flat head, small eyes on top, long whiskers and chin barbels made of thin cubes, pale belly. Rig: root > body (front segment) > body_mid > body_rear > tail_fin for the side-to-side swim wave; body > head > jaw; pectoral fins fin_r / fin_l.\n\n- Cubes: 17 (all unrotated unless noted). Texture 64x64, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Rest bounds (body, no held items): x -19.5..19.5, y 0.0..16.0, z -36.5..32.0 (faces -Z).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 9.0 x 15.4 x 64.0 (w x h x d) centred on x = 0, z = 0, from y = 0 (belly)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `swim` | 1.4 | loop | body wave travelling to the tail (loop, played in place) |\n| `idle` | 2.4 | loop | gentle hover: slow wave, fins sculling, gills/jaw pulse (loop) |\n| `dart` | 0.5 | loop | fast flee, big tail beats, fins tucked (loop) |\n| `flop` | 1.2 | loop | caught, on land: lies on its right side and slaps up and down (loop) |\n| `death` | 2 | hold | rolls belly-up and holds; rests on y = 0 (the game can float it at the water surface) |\n\n## Move speeds (in-place cycles; stride matched to these)\n\n- `swim`: 17.8 u/s (0.5 m/s), wave cycle 1.4 s\n- `dart`: 71.1 u/s (2.0 m/s), wave cycle 0.5 s\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups, pivot in model units)\n\n\n## Variant textures (same UV layout)\n\n- `fish_giant_catfish_young.png`: young fish texture (use at half scale): paler, softer markings\n\n## Notes\n\n- Fish rest with the lowest fin on y = 0 so the same model lies correctly on land; in water the game sets the depth.\n"},"description":"# fish_giant_catfish\n\nGiant catfish (B8), 1.8 m (64 u). Deepwoods pools.\n\nDark mottled grey-green, wide flat head, small eyes on top, long whiskers and chin barbels made of thin cubes, pale belly. Rig: root > body (front segment) > body_mid > body_rear > tail_fin for the side-to-side swim wave; body > head > jaw; pectoral fins fin_r / fin_l.\n\n- Cubes: 17 (all unrotated unless noted). Texture 64x64, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Rest bounds (body, no held items): x -19.5..19.5, y 0.0..16.0, z -36.5..32.0 (faces -Z).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 9.0 x 15.4 x 64.0 (w x h x d) centred on x = 0, z = 0, from y = 0 (belly)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `swim` | 1.4 | loop | body wave travelling to the tail (loop, played in place) |\n| `idle` | 2.4 | loop | gentle hover: slow wave, fins sculling, gills/jaw pulse (loop) |\n| `dart` | 0.5 | loop | fast flee, big tail beats, fins tucked (loop) |\n| `flop` | 1.2 | loop | caught, on land: lies on its right side and slaps up and down (loop) |\n| `death` | 2 | hold | rolls belly-up and holds; rests on y = 0 (the game can float it at the water surface) |\n\n## Move speeds (in-place cycles; stride matched to these)\n\n- `swim`: 17.8 u/s (0.5 m/s), wave cycle 1.4 s\n- `dart`: 71.1 u/s (2.0 m/s), wave cycle 0.5 s\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups, pivot in model units)\n\n\n## Variant textures (same UV layout)\n\n- `fish_giant_catfish_young.png`: young fish texture (use at half scale): paler, softer markings\n\n## Notes\n\n- Fish rest with the lowest fin on y = 0 so the same model lies correctly on land; in water the game sets the depth.\n","resolution":{"width":64,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"head","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-8.0,1.0,-32.0],"to":[8.0,9.75,-17.75],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,7.0,-19.5],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[11,54,27.0,62.75],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[43,54,57.25,62.75],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[27,54,43.0,